  <h2 id="sales">Who pays for these skills, and how they judge you</h2>

  <p>
    Employers screen quickly and test claims in interviews. They judge you by clarity, honesty and proof.
  </p>
  <p>
    The first basic skill is writing one line that shows what you did with a tool.
  </p>

  <h2 id="ai">AI and listing computer Excel and language skills on a resume: which tasks are under pressure</h2>

  <p>
    AI tools can help phrase lines and check spelling. Routine formatting shrinks.
  </p>
  <p>
    Honest self-assessment and proof hold value. A staged path helps: now, use AI to phrase and check; later, let your work speak.
  </p>

